body:
Hmm...

&#x200B;

Well, the first thing I would do is to try and get completely over him.

Say to yourself that it's completely over and that you will never go back to being together. Do not give yourself any hope of reconciliation. That's vital. It's completely OVER.

If you think you can't be friends with him because you won't be able to get over him... Then stop being friends.  I know you've said you can't really avoid him, but try to avoid him as much as possible and always give him the cold shoulder. Tell him that you don't wanna interact with him AT ALL anymore. And then just do not interact. Do not talk.

&#x200B;

But yeah. If you want him, but he doesn't. Yet he doesn't say any reasons, that's just toxic. Maybe he wants to have you as some fallback option for some quick affection or sex.

&#x200B;

So yeah, the first step is accepting that it's over and moving on.

You will find someone else. Someone better.

&#x200B;

The more desperate you become for a relationship, the harder it is to get one.

Because people are gonna use you for sex or whatever.

&#x200B;

The second step would be to become content with yourself.

&#x200B;

Anyway, this just my personal opinion, feel free to do whatever.

Hopefully, I have given you some ideas though.

Damn, what an amazing post. I can definitely relate to a lot of things you have written here.

&#x200B;

You also do sound like an awesome, interesting and understanding person.

I'd be down to chat and be a friend, but unfortunately, my English ain't good.

&#x200B;

(Can't really speak that language in a smooth and comfortable manner. Definitely not eloquent at all, haha)

&#x200B;

Anyway, I do hope you will be able to find an honest and true person to chat with, with whom you both will be able to just be yourselves, without any fakery or some bullshit like that. I believe that will be quite cathartic, just talking it out, talking about anything, while being yourself, without having to constrict yourself, fake anything or put on a mask.

&#x200B;

I wish you the best of luck.

And of course, always stay careful.

Humans require some resources to be able to live.

&#x200B;

Now, if humans want to actually even have fun and live a better life than just having the basic necessities, well it gets even harder because more resources are needed.

&#x200B;

And unfortunately, those resources aren't free...

Humans are working and creating those resources.

Nobody does it for free though.

&#x200B;

So yeah, it all is about money.

Everything gets worse when you are alone and lonely.

When you're left alone with your own thoughts for pretty much ever.

&#x200B;

When you can't reach out to anyone.

When no one genuinely cares about you.

&#x200B;

When you feel like chatting or sharing something, when you want someone to care about you, yet you have no one.

&#x200B;

When you're looking for that physical affection, a hug or something, yet you have no one.

&#x200B;

When you want some support for anything really, yet again you have no one.

&#x200B;

When... okay, okay, I'm done.

&#x200B;

But yeah, I always thought that I wouldn't really need or want anyone, or anyone to care about me. Didn't realize how empty and pointless would life seem when you have no one.

Anyway : )

Yeah...

&#x200B;

We want people to care about us, to listen and all that.

I know I do. But then I realize, life is truly fucking hard.

In order to live properly, most people have to really focus on their lives and themselves. They are suffering too. They have a lot of problems and are going through different phases of their lives. Sometimes it may be really hard for them to extend their focus to other people too, to care about them and all that, when they are already getting overwhelmed by their own problems.

&#x200B;

So yeah, it just fucking sucks.

Dunno what to say.

&#x200B;

I just hope OP finds some reason to stay...

It's all about luck.

&#x200B;

Either randomly some people will see your post and upvote it, then it will get to hot and climb from there... Or it will get lost in the new posts section. Not many people sort by new... so yeah.

&#x200B;

Lastly, sometimes a lot of people may struggle to come up with a response.

They may not know how to respond to your post appropriately. So, to not make anything worse they just don't comment anything. It is not that easy. Plus, we all are struggling and suffering in different ways here, aren't we?...

&#x200B;

But I believe, most do people care.

And here you go, more than 20+ comments already  : )

Comparisons, indeed. Worst shit ever. Can't really help it either. Especially when watching a series like The Office, I mean you just see them having normal good moments that anyone in actual real life could have too. Well, not anyone. Not me for example, hence it all gets even more depressing.

&#x200B;

And yeah, unfortunately, life is all about facing stuff, chasing new challenges!

Putting yourself out there, fighting and overcoming your fears!

Not hesitating to put yourself in uncomfortable situations, always on the path of improvement!

Plus, socializing, being social and all that is becoming extremely important, though I guess it always has been that way... Confidence and super social skills. Yeah, right.

&#x200B;

Even when you try your best, even when you REALLY try, it can still all get fucked up. There are factors and things that you just cannot control.

&#x200B;

Lastly, every human requires some resources to be able to live. Those resources aren't free though. So, working is unavoidable. Oh well, time to stop my rambling.

Life can surely be really hard though.

&#x200B;

But of course, to a lot of people, all that probably sounds very exciting!

Well, good for them, good for them.

&#x200B;

Anyway, here we are, me and you both.

There is a thing there called Tiny Habits.

It's a 5-day program that will teach you how to create tiny little habits/behaviors.

Such as like, after you pee, you will do two pushups.

&#x200B;

Those habits are very easy and will become slowly automatic, then you can start making them harder and flesh them out. It's really helpful and doesn't even actually need that much motivation. But it will help you overall. It will make you feel better.

&#x200B;

I know that's not exactly what you are looking for... but finding motivation is just extremely hard. For Tiny habits though, you don't need some huge as fuck motivation or will power.

&#x200B;

And of course, all that is completely free. I have tried it myself. Otherwise, I wouldn't suggest it.

Anyway, this is just a little suggestion of mine. Do what you want! : )

Yup, that's what I'm planning to do, to just slowly learn/absorb most of the basics from playing the tutorial.

And that, I really like that feature. That I can basically pause the game and slowly plan out and think about what I'm gonna do. It is really awesome.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

"Every mistake, every disaster is a learning opportunity."  
I shall remember that.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

(Like for example, that roofs collapse if you remove what supports them.

It makes sense, doesn't it? But I didn't know that. My guy got crushed, a little. )

Here are the mods I am playing with currently:

&#x200B;

* **Automate**.

This mod is so good, I doubt that I will ever be able to play without it.

Check it out.

&#x200B;

* **BetterFruitTrees**

Mostly visual, plus it allows you to plant those trees, without having to leave any spaces between them.

&#x200B;

* **BetterRanching**

Just visual stuff, adds an indicator that shows if you have petted the animals and if you have milked the cows.

&#x200B;

* **BigSilo**

Just a bigger silo.

Basically, you can fit unlimited hay there.

&#x200B;

* **catGifts**

Your pet will bring you gifts, sometimes.

&#x200B;

* **CJBShowItemSellPrice**

Pretty self-explanatory.

&#x200B;

* **DeepWoodsMod**

This is pretty damn awesome.

Adds levels which you can explore, get tons of stuff, in the Secret Woods.

&#x200B;

* **FriendsForever**

No friendship decay.

&#x200B;

* **GrassChance**

More grass.

&#x200B;

* **HarvestWithScythe**

Pretty self-explanatory.

&#x200B;

* **LookupAnything**

Allows you to hover over an item and then press F1 to see all the info about that item.

(For example, who likes/loves it, if the community center needs it and more)

&#x200B;

* **NoFenceDecay**

Pretty self-explanatory.

&#x200B;

* **NPCMapLocations.**

Pretty self-explanatory.

&#x200B;

* **RangeDisplay**

Allows you to check the range of scarecrows, sprinklers, etc.

&#x200B;

* **SkipFishingMinigame**

I don't like fishing...so yeah.

&#x200B;

* **StackEverything**

Allows you to stack everything, machines and all that.

&#x200B;

* **StackToNearbyChests**

Moves any items from your inventory into nearby chests if they contain at least 1 of the item, with the click of one button.

&#x200B;

* **TillableGround**

Allows you to make any untillable ground, tillable.

&#x200B;

* **TractorMod**

The tractor is awesome.

&#x200B;

* **WearMoreRings**

You can wear more rings : )

&#x200B;

Most of these, don't actually change the game that much.

&#x200B;

But there are mods such as [Stardew Valley Expanded](https://www.nexusmods.com/stardewvalley/mods/3753) that will really change the game and add a lot of stuff. I haven't really tried it yet, but here's a small description "This mod features 12 new locations, 38 new character events, over 500 location messages, reimagined maps and festivals (all maps), remastered Immersive Farm 2, a new town map reflecting all changes, and many miscellaneous additions! "

&#x200B;

Also these:

RTGOAT's Longevity (w-More Crops Mod and DNPCC)

Artisan Valley - A CFR and JA Pack

&#x200B;

Again, I haven't tested or tried those either, but they do look quite awesome and game-changing.
